From 3b127c950f127489c4719073124c2a297a1636d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:49:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Ask for a pairing file only when none is in place

SideStore's launch starts minimuxer with the pairing file and asks the
iPhone for its UDID through LocalDevVPN. When the iPhone did not answer,
LocalDevVPN being off as often as not, minimuxer reported an invalid
pairing file, and the launch screen asked for another one (Pairing File
Required), although the file Cartouche's setup had put in place was the
right one. In Cartouche the pairing file is Cartouche's to put in place
and to replace, from its setup: the launch now asks for a file only when
none is there. Settings still imports one by hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 SideStore/AppBootManager.swift | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/SideStore/AppBootManager.swift b/SideStore/AppBootManager.swift
index ec9becb..fd230a4 100644
--- a/SideStore/AppBootManager.swift
+++ b/SideStore/AppBootManager.swift
@@ -51,7 +51,11 @@ public final class AppBootManager {
         } catch {
             if case MinimuxerError.invalidPairing = error {
                 debugLog("[AppBootManager] startMinimuxer(): Minimuxer fetchUDID() based connection test FAILED. \(error)")
-                self.needsPairingPrompt = true
+                // Cartouche: the pairing file is Cartouche's to put in place
+                // and to replace, from its setup (CartouchePairing), and the
+                // iPhone's silence here is as often LocalDevVPN's as the
+                // file's. The launch asks for a file only when none is in
+                // place (performBootSequence).
                 throw error
             } else {
                 debugLog("[AppBootManager] startMinimuxer(): Minimuxer fetchUDID() based connection test FAILED but PAIRING FILE IS VALID. \(error)")
-- 
